% Quoting and escaping. Getting any of this wrong is an injection, not a
% formatting nit, which is why it is the first file.

### name: lex.number.canonical-form-survives
--- note
2.50 keeps its scale: scale is part of a SEL number and part of what SQL
DECIMAL arithmetic reads. Reformatting it would change the value.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
2.50
--- expect
2.50
===
### name: lex.number.leading-zeros-canonicalised-by-the-parser
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
007
--- expect
7
===
### name: lex.number.negative-is-an-operator-not-a-literal
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
-5
--- expect
